    <string name="notification_access_guide_title">Limit what Taxi Plate can read</string>
    <string name="notification_access_guide_body">1. Use the package switches under Notification adapters. Taxi Plate checks them before notification text reaches parsing or diagnostics. The switch covers notifications Android delivers from personal, work, and private profiles.\n\n2. The button below opens Android’s notification-access details specifically for Taxi Plate. You can also revoke access completely there.\n\n3. Taxi Plate’s system page has four categories: Notifications, Conversations, Real-time, and Silent. Open See all apps to allow or block notification delivery from each app for this listener. These Android controls are the system-level boundary; the package switches inside Taxi Plate provide an additional filter.\n\n4. Keep Taxi Plate in the personal profile. Android does not run notification listeners inside a work profile, and a work administrator may block notifications from crossing profiles.\n\n5. Private Space is separate and is stopped while locked. Taxi Plate can process private-profile notifications only when Android exposes them to the personal-profile listener.</string>
